<p>Damn if you didn't find a good picture to work with…</p>
<p>Agreed with both of the above:<br />
I wouldn't do any experiments with it… but it's begging for a pre-containment incident report.<br />
The article doesn't give any reason that the average, non-pregnant female would be particularly threatened here.</p>
<p>Finally:<br />
" and the characters are equal to a known early dialect of Japanese."</p>
<p>Imma put on my grammar Nazi cap for a minute… equal isn't quite right for this since it's usually used for quantities, it's like saying "they are equal in appearance".<br />
I'd suggest: similar, identical, comparable, etc.<br />
or even "and the characters have been identified as a known early dialect of Japanese."</p>
<p>Overall it's compelling, and when I first saw the picture I thought "oh sh*t, here we go". But the effects aren't quite compelling enough without hearing more about that demon…</p>
<p>EDIT:<br />
"Baby we don't need to use that this time, I scheduled you to do some testing with 051 tomorrow."<br />
-Dr. █████'s file titled "Things NOT to say to research assistants"</p>

