			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1424228">
									

<p>This was very nice and creepy.</p>
<p>The only bit I think could use more details is in the interview. It resumes to 'child looked very much deformed, looked at doctor, laughed at doctor, doctor snapped his neck'. Did everyone present see the child presumably stillborn, but laughing? Nurse is mentioned to have seen it but isn't specified what exactly she saw. Did everyone present consider it was alright that the doctor just went on and snapped the child's neck? Did seeing and touching the child affect the doctor in any way in his future?</p>
<p>I don't think this is something that leads people to think more about things, but is merely lack of details. And that's a thin line there. However, if this was intended, my apologies.</p>

